Article 7 (Metropolitan Transport Policy Bureau)
(1) The Metropolitan Transport Policy Bureau shall have one Director General, who shall be appointed from among general service public officials belonging to the Senior Executive Service.
(2) The Director General of the Metropolitan Transport Policy Bureau shall take charge of the following matters:
1. General coordination of metropolitan transport policies;
2. Support for formulation of the basic plan for metropolitan transport;
3. Formulation and implementation of metropolitan transport implementation plans;
4. Matters concerning annual implementation plans for metropolitan transport implementation plans;
5. Establishment and implementation of measures to improve metropolitan transport;
6. Operation of the metropolitan transport facilities charge system;
7. Submission and follow-up management of agenda items for the Commission, the working committee under Article 9 (4) of the Act, and regional committees under Article 9-5 of the Act;
8. Establishment of plans and route coordination for metropolitan public transportation in metropolitan areas;
9. Management of operators of metropolitan express-type and direct-seat-type city buses (hereinafter referred to as "metropolitan buses") in metropolitan areas;
10. Matters concerning semi-public operation systems for metropolitan buses in metropolitan areas;
11. Management of metropolitan bus workers and operation and safety management of vehicles, facilities, etc.;
12. Efficiency of metropolitan bus dispatching and service-level management, including reservation systems;
13. Matters concerning reduction of transportation costs, including operation of metropolitan public transportation pass and discount systems;
14. Integration and coordination of taxi business zones in metropolitan areas;
15. Matters concerning fares, including standards for basic fares of metropolitan buses and transfer settlement methods;
16. Consultation and disputes concerning connecting transportation among urban railway operators, railway operators, etc. in metropolitan areas;
17. Collection and management of metropolitan transport information in metropolitan areas.
